A49. You may have to go over via this on your next crossing. ~ DUCT
A50. Alfred the Great & Co. ~ LUNTS
A51. Vitamin D—found in Vegetable Diets. ~ VD
A52. A high monk. ~ APE
A53. This man never wrote—he wired on the dot with lots of dash. ~ MORSE
A54. So far, there is no law against this keeping open till all hours. ~ EYELID
A56. Kept a good balance. ~ POISED
A57. She expected a solitaire but he gave her this ring on April 1st. ~ TELEPHONE

D1. You can't resist this kind of man. ~ ARMED
D2. Her ladyship was tied to this. ~ PEER
D3. The house of a thousand scandals (abbr. plur.) ~ RDS
D4. Follow a "be" line for this. ~ IS
D5. Threshers. ~ FLAILS
D6. All slicked up. ~ OILED
D7. These little things add up into big things. ~ ONES
